    "title": "Trump's mail voting order hits another legal wall - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gesi Lloyd ,\n9 hours ago A federal judge in Washington has blocked the U.S. Postal Service from carrying out proposed restrictions on mail-in ballot delivery, ruling that the plan violated a legal settlement the agency reached with the NAACP years earlier. The decision marks the second time in as many weeks that a court has stopped a piece of President Trump’s push to overhaul mail-in voting ahead of the November midterms. Read full article",
